@startuml cmp_tcu_software_parts
title TCU software parts and memory regions (DC-04, reprogramming sections 1, 5 .. 7)

left to right direction

component "MCU-Link SWD (E-07)\ndebugger" as Dbg
component "PBL (E-02)\nprimary bootloader, separate image,\nupdated by debugger only" as PBL
component "Application (E-04)\nseparate image, written by the SBL" as App
component "SBL (E-03)\nsecondary bootloader, separate image,\ndownloaded for each programming session" as SBL

package "Flash bank 0 (8 KiB sectors, 16-byte phrases)" {
  database "PBL region\n0x0000_0000 .. 0x0000_FFFF (64 KiB)" as FlashPbl
  database "Boot info A 0x0001_0000 .. 0x0001_1FFF\nBoot info B 0x0001_2000 .. 0x0001_3FFF\nI-17b boot info record: magic, sequence,\nfingerprint (F15A), programming counter (FD00), CRC" as FlashBi
  database "Application header 0x0001_4000 .. 0x0001_43FF (1 KiB)\nI-17a image header: magic, header_crc32, hw_id 0x0947_0001,\nsw_version, image_size, image_crc32, min_pbl_version" as FlashHdr
  database "Application image (vector table first)\n0x0001_4400 .. 0x000F_FFFF (943 KiB)" as FlashImg
}
database "Flash bank 1\n0x0010_0000 .. 0x001F_FFFF\nreserved" as FlashB1

package "RAM" {
  database "SBL load area (SRAMX) 0x0400_0000 .. 0x0400_FFFF (64 KiB)\nSBL bss + stack 0x0401_0000 .. 0x0401_7FFF" as Sramx
  database "PBL / application RAM\n0x2000_0000 .. 0x2006_7FFF (416 KiB)" as SysRam
}

PBL --> SBL : 31 01 03 01: starts the SBL;\nI-17c hand-over in RAM: programming session,\nsecurity unlocked, CAN configuration

PBL ..> FlashHdr : reads I-17a at every start\n(SYS-BOOT-001, SYS-BOOT-013)
PBL ..> FlashImg : reads for the image CRC32
PBL ..> FlashBi : reads newest valid slot (DIDs)
PBL --> Sramx : writes the SBL image with 36,\nonly inside the load area (reprogramming 11.1)
PBL ..> SysRam : uses

App ..> FlashHdr : reads sw_version (DID F181)
App ..> FlashBi : reads (DIDs)
App ..> SysRam : uses

SBL ..> Sramx : runs only from RAM (RB-04)
SBL --> FlashHdr : erase / write (SYS-BOOT-004); writes the header\nsector last, after 0202 / FF01 passed (SYS-BOOT-015)
SBL --> FlashImg : erase / write (SYS-BOOT-004)
SBL --> FlashBi : writes the slot that is not the newest
SBL ..> FlashPbl : erase / write refused, NRC 31 (SYS-BOOT-006)
SBL ..> FlashB1 : erase / write refused, NRC 31 (SYS-BOOT-006)

Dbg --> FlashPbl : flash PBL, no mass erase (SYS-BOOT-006, RB-06)
Dbg --> FlashHdr : flash application with a valid header (RB-06)

note top of SBL
Covers: SYS-BOOT-001, SYS-BOOT-004, SYS-BOOT-006, SYS-BOOT-013, SYS-BOOT-015
Only the SBL erases or writes flash (DC-04, SYS-BOOT-004); the PBL and the
application never do (verified by review of the map files).
No RAM content is kept across a reset (reprogramming sections 5, 8).
end note
@enduml
